**[W1&Q1] Limited analysis of template evolution dynamics: Do templates converge? Are they interpretable?**

We appreciate the reviewer’s insightful question in examining how the scoring templates evolve throughout the outer loop and their interpretability. Through the additional analyses on AdvBench with Claude-3.5-Haiku as the target model, we observe both **(1) consistent convergence and (2) clear structural patterns in the templates.** 

**(1) Convergence**: In the table below, we computed ROUGE and BLEU similarities between consecutive templates to quantify template changes. The largest shift occurs in the first iterations (π_0→π_1), reflecting the initial exploration phase (e.g., ROUGE-L: 0.29, BLEU: 8.7). After this point, template similarities increase substantially and become stable (e.g., ROUGE-L: 0.46–0.61, BLEU: 25–37), showing incremental updates. This trajectory indicates a predictable “explore → refine → converge” pattern. Full statistics are provided in Appendix Table 17.

